1. What is Metadata?

Metadata is information about a document/chunk, rather than the actual document content.

For example:

Document:
"FastAPI is a Python web framework..."

Metadata:
{
    "file_name": "backend_notes.pdf",
    "file_type": "pdf",
    "folder": "D:/Projects/AI",
    "author": "Arun",
    "year": 2026
}

The actual text is:

FastAPI is a Python web framework...

Metadata describes it:

file_name = backend_notes.pdf
file_type = pdf
folder = AI
year = 2026

2. Why do we need Metadata Filtering?

Imagine your desktop has:

Documents/
│
├── resume.pdf
├── fastapi_notes.pdf
├── docker_notes.pdf
├── company_policy.pdf
├── vacation.pdf
├── finance.xlsx
└── project.docx

User asks:

"What does the company policy say about leave?"

Without filtering:

All documents
    ↓
Embedding search
    ↓
Find relevant chunks

With metadata:

file_type = pdf
folder = company

we can narrow the search first.

All documents
     ↓
Metadata filter
     ↓
Relevant subset
     ↓
Semantic search
     ↓
Top-K